<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#canadian-red-ensign">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canadian Red Ensign</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Canadian Red Ensign was a red flag with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-flag">Union Jack</a> in the canton and the Canadian coat of arms in the fly, used as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s unofficial and later official national flag on land and at sea from the late nineteenth century. Canadian forces fought under it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. It was replaced by the Maple Leaf flag on 15 February 1965.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canadian-red-ensign.jpg" alt="Canadian Red Ensign" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Denelson83 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Canada_(1957%E2%80%931965).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
